Maintainer-Entscheidung 2026-09-30: SDKs mit Platzhalter-Key (Bearer dummy) unter --from-env bekommen seit k47/k52 fuer entdeckte Modelle 401 vom Provider. Neu: antwortet der Upstream bei raw passthrough eines NUR auto-discovered Modells mit 401 (vor dem ersten weitergeleiteten Byte -- beim Streaming kommt der Status vor dem Body), wird der Request transparent ueber die Engine (Handler::Router, Knarrs Key) beantwortet; Client merkt nichts. Nicht fuer unbekannte (nicht discovered) Modelle und nicht fuer explizit konfigurierte. Body des Requests muss dafuer gepuffert vorliegen (ist er). Tracing: ein Trace, Fallback im Metadata vermerken. Native + PSGI, sync + stream. Tests. Doku.

2026-09-30 03:57 Design: raw path decides on the upstream status before anything reaches the client (native sync on_done, native stream on_header, PSGI after the buffered get). A 401 for a request that may fall back (raw passthrough of a model the router resolves = discovered-only) notes extra->{passthrough_fallback}=401 on the parsed Request and answers it through the handler chain (Handler::Router -> engine, Knarr key); the upstream's 401 body is drained and dropped. One trace: the raw trace of a fallback-eligible request is started only once the status rules the fallback out (Tracing start_trace gets start_hires to keep its start time); on fallback the handler chain's Handler::Tracing trace is the one trace and carries metadata passthrough_fallback=401. Other statuses unchanged. Knarr.pm: tail of _action_chat moved into _handle_chat (pure move) so the fallback can reuse it.

